+# Broadcom research record
+
+Accessed 2026-08-15. These live sources were consulted independently of the pinned grading snapshot.
+
+- **Upgrading VMware Aria Operations 8.x to VCF Operations 9.0 using VMware Aria Suite Lifecycle**
+  <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/433805/upgrading-vmware-aria-operations-8x-to-v.html>
+  Used to confirm the Operations upgrade workflow, required binaries and prechecks, Fleet Management deployment, and the VCF-versus-other entitlement branch.
+
+- **Import and upgrade VMware Aria Automation 8.x to VCF Automation 9.0**
+  <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/433806/import-and-upgrade-vmware-aria-automatio.html>
+  Used to confirm that the legacy Automation instance is imported from Aria Suite Lifecycle into VCF Operations Fleet Management before its upgrade is triggered.
+
+- **Update sequence for VCF 9.0 and compatible VMware products**
+  <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html>
+  Used to confirm the ordering of Lifecycle, Operations/Fleet Management, Automation, and Logs; the Lifecycle 8.18 Patch 2 prerequisite; the fresh Logs deployment; and the 90-day log-data transfer boundary.
+
+- **Upgrade Guidance for Aria Operations for Logs 8.18.x to VCF Operations for Logs 9.0.x**
+  <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/402314>
+  Used to confirm there is no in-place Logs upgrade, parallel operation is supported, integrations must be reconfigured, and at most 90 days of log data can be transferred.
+
+- **Getting started with VMware Cloud Foundation (VCF) or VMware vSphere Foundation (VVF) V9 Licensing**
+  <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/437242/getting-started-with-vmware-cloud-founda.html>
+  Used to confirm that version 9 licensing is registered through VCF Operations and that one license allocation cannot be used by two VCF Operations instances.
+
+- **No License message or evaluation mode in VMware Cloud Foundation Operations for Logs 9.0**
+  <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/404339/>
